DESCRIPTION:Duration: 97 mins (1h37m)\n\nSet in Caracas during the 2017 pr
 otests\, this gripping social thriller follows a woman trapped in a city c
 onsumed by repression and chaos. When regime loyalists seize her apartment
 \, she is forced into hiding and begins to hatch a desperate plan in a per
 ilous bid to escape the country.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/it-would
 -be-night-in-caracas\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Downtown (Fri 15 May\, 12:
 30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 18:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chili Finger
DTSTART:20260517T041500Z
DTEND:20260517T060500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T041500Z
UID:k6alrciddk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nWhen a human finger is accidenta
 lly served in a cup of fast-food chili\, the restaurant\, its horrified cu
 stomers\, and the digitless victim all scramble over who gets blamed\, and
  who gets paid\, in this queasy black comedy. Directors Edd Benda and Step
 hen Helstad scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/chili-fi
 nger\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Downtown (Wed 13 May\, 9:30 PM)\n\nEstimat
 ed start: 21:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Furious
DTSTART:20260517T065900Z
DTEND:20260517T090400Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T065900Z
UID:wehJX6Q0ql
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nAfter the daughter of Wang Wei (
 Xie Miao) is kidnapped by a criminal network and he receives no help from 
 the corrupt police\, Wei sets out on a rampage to find her himself. His on
 ly ally is Navin (Joe Taslim) – a relentless journalist whose wife has m
 ysteriously disappeared. Fueled by a furious vengeance\, the unlikely duo 
 ruthlessly fights against the kidnappers in this explosive martial arts sh
 owdown.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-furious\n\nAlso playing at:\n
   • Uptown House 2 (Sun 17 May\, 7:45 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 0:09
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Prisoners of the Earth (1939)
DTSTART:20260517T203000Z
DTEND:20260517T221000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T203000Z
UID:34eG8ty9KR
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 86 mins (1h26m)\n\nThe most acclaimed film by one of
  classic Argentine cinema’s foremost directors is a gut-punching work of
  social realism: a group of desperate men are conscripted to labor on a tr
 eacherous plantation—a situation that boils over in an explosive act of 
 rebellion.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/prisoners-of-the-earth\n\nEsti
 mated start: 13:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sundays
DTSTART:20260517T230000Z
DTEND:20260518T011000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T230000Z
UID:9gKSXh34CY
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 117 mins (1h57m)\n\nAt 17\, Ainara faces a life-chan
 ging choice: after high school\, she considers becoming a nun. Her decisio
 n unsettles her family\, especially her aunt Montse\, who fears it means l
 osing freedom. The year's Goya Award standout offers a stirring tale about
  the fragile balance between faith and skepticism.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net
 /festival/sundays\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Downtown (Thu 14 May\, 3:30 P
 M)\n\nEstimated start: 16:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Invite
DTSTART:20260518T020000Z
DTEND:20260518T040500Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T020000Z
UID:g2wD31Ftqe
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 107 mins (1h47m)\n\nJoe and Angela’s marriage is o
 n thin ice. When they invite their enigmatic upstairs neighbors for a dinn
 er party\, the night spirals into unexpected places. Have they reignited t
 he spark or lit the match that burns it all down? Director & star Olivia 
 Wilde scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-invite\n\n
 Estimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
